IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il37-nouns`

-- Basic Law: The Judiciary, ss 4, 4A, 4B, 7(4) and Amendment No. 4 s 3 (commencement and application). Row IL-37.
-- Target compiler: main. Every rule takes a vintage or a tally as an input; the two texts are never merged.
-- Numbering: the Hebrew letter of a subsection is glossed as (a) for (א), (b) for (ב), (c) for (ג), (d) for (ד), (e) for (ה), (f) for (ו).
-- Hebrew is quoted only in comments, copied from the instrument or the consolidation named; where the consolidation and the instrument differ, the instrument is what is encoded.
--
-- Reading a result. A BOOLEAN answers "is it so on these facts". A MAYBE is JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE where the text answers and NOTHING where the text is silent.

§ `Section 4: the committee`

§§ `Who sits (s 4(b))`

-- s 4(b) before the 26th Knesset (the consolidation's undated text; the instrument's s 1(1) replaced it):
--   הועדה תהיה של תשעה חברים, שהם נשיא בית המשפט העליון, שני שופטים אחרים של בית המשפט העליון שיבחר חבר שופטיו, שר המשפטים ושר אחר שתקבע הממשלה,
--   שני חברי הכנסת שתבחר הכנסת ושני נציגים של לשכת עורכי הדין שתבחר המועצה הארצית של הלשכה; שר המשפטים יהיה יושב ראש הועדה.
-- s 4(b)(1) from the 26th Knesset (SH 3388 p. 434, read from the page image): nine members, namely (a) the President of the Supreme Court and two other justices;
--   (b) the Minister of Justice and another minister; (c) two Knesset members, one of the coalition factions and one of the opposition factions;
--   (d) two public representatives, one chosen by the coalition Knesset members and one by the opposition Knesset members.
-- s 4(f)(2): where the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members, the Knesset chooses both public representatives.
@ref Basic Law: The Judiciary s 4(b), s 4(b)(1), s 4(f)(2); SH 3388 p. 434
GIVEN vintage IS A `A vintage of the committee rule`
      `the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `A seat on the committee`
`the seats of the committee` MEANS
    CONSIDER vintage
    WHEN `the text before the 26th Knesset` THEN `the seats before the 26th Knesset`
    WHEN `the transitional window of Amendment No. 4 section 3` THEN `the seats before the 26th Knesset`
    WHEN `the text from the 26th Knesset` THEN
        IF `the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members`
        THEN LIST `the President of the Supreme Court`,
                  `another justice of the Supreme Court whom the body of its justices chose`,
                  `another justice of the Supreme Court whom the body of its justices chose`,
                  `the Minister of Justice`,
                  `another minister whom the Government names`,
                  `the Knesset member of the coalition factions`,
                  `the Knesset member of the opposition factions`,
                  `a public representative whom the Knesset as a whole chose`,
                  `a public representative whom the Knesset as a whole chose`
        ELSE LIST `the President of the Supreme Court`,
                  `another justice of the Supreme Court whom the body of its justices chose`,
                  `another justice of the Supreme Court whom the body of its justices chose`,
                  `the Minister of Justice`,
                  `another minister whom the Government names`,
                  `the Knesset member of the coalition factions`,
                  `the Knesset member of the opposition factions`,
                  `the public representative whom the coalition Knesset members chose`,
                  `the public representative whom the opposition Knesset members chose`

GIVETH A LIST OF `A seat on the committee`
`the seats before the 26th Knesset` MEANS
    LIST `the President of the Supreme Court`,
         `another justice of the Supreme Court whom the body of its justices chose`,
         `another justice of the Supreme Court whom the body of its justices chose`,
         `the Minister of Justice`,
         `another minister whom the Government names`,
         `a Knesset member whom the Knesset chose`,
         `a Knesset member whom the Knesset chose`,
         `a representative of the Bar Association`,
         `a representative of the Bar Association`

-- The Minister of Justice is the chair (s 4(b)(2) from the 26th Knesset; the last words of s 4(b) before).
@ref Basic Law: The Judiciary s 4(b)(2)
GIVEN seat IS A `A seat on the committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the seat chairs the committee` MEANS
    seat EQUALS `the Minister of Justice`

§§ `Which paragraph of s 4(d) a seat is in`

-- s 4(d) from the 26th Knesset: paragraph (1) a judge; (2) a minister, a Knesset member of the coalition factions or the public representative the coalition Knesset members chose;
-- (3) a Knesset member of the opposition factions or the public representative the opposition Knesset members chose. The public representative whom the Knesset as a whole chose
-- (s 4(f)(2)) is named in none of the three, so such a member counts toward the five and toward no paragraph (fork D2 in NOTES.md).
@ref Basic Law: The Judiciary s 4(d)(1), (2), (3); SH 3388 p. 434
GIVEN seat IS A `A seat on the committee`
GIVETH A `A paragraph of section 4(d)`
`the paragraph of section 4(d) that a seat is in` MEANS
    CONSIDER seat
    WHEN `the President of the Supreme Court` THEN `paragraph 1, a judge`
    WHEN `another justice of the Supreme Court whom the body of its justices chose` THEN `paragraph 1, a judge`
    WHEN `the Minister of Justice` THEN `paragraph 2, a minister, a Knesset member of the coalition factions, or the public representative the coalition Knesset members chose`
    WHEN `another minister whom the Government names` THEN `paragraph 2, a minister, a Knesset member of the coalition factions, or the public representative the coalition Knesset members chose`
    WHEN `the Knesset member of the coalition factions` THEN `paragraph 2, a minister, a Knesset member of the coalition factions, or the public representative the coalition Knesset members chose`
    WHEN `the public representative whom the coalition Knesset members chose` THEN `paragraph 2, a minister, a Knesset member of the coalition factions, or the public representative the coalition Knesset members chose`
    WHEN `the Knesset member of the opposition factions` THEN `paragraph 3, a Knesset member of the opposition factions, or the public representative the opposition Knesset members chose`
    WHEN `the public representative whom the opposition Knesset members chose` THEN `paragraph 3, a Knesset member of the opposition factions, or the public representative the opposition Knesset members chose`
    WHEN `a representative of the Bar Association` THEN `none of the three paragraphs`
    WHEN `a Knesset member whom the Knesset chose` THEN `none of the three paragraphs`
    WHEN `a public representative whom the Knesset as a whole chose` THEN `none of the three paragraphs`

-- s 4(f)(1): the three members that are the two ministers and the Knesset member of the coalition factions.
@ref Basic Law: The Judiciary s 4(f)(1)
GIVEN seat IS A `A seat on the committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the seat is one of the three of section 4(f)(1)` MEANS
    seat EQUALS `the Minister of Justice`
    OR seat EQUALS `another minister whom the Government names`
    OR seat EQUALS `the Knesset member of the coalition factions`

§§ `Counting a tally`

GIVEN members IS A LIST OF `A member serving on the committee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number of members serving` MEANS
    CONSIDER members
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN m FOLLOWED BY rest THEN 1 PLUS `the number of members serving` rest

GIVEN members IS A LIST OF `A member serving on the committee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number voting in favour` MEANS
    CONSIDER members
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN m FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (IF m's `votes in favour` THEN 1 ELSE 0) PLUS `the number voting in favour` rest

GIVEN members IS A LIST OF `A member serving on the committee`
      paragraph IS A `A paragraph of section 4(d)`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number in favour from a paragraph of section 4(d)` MEANS
    CONSIDER members
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN m FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (IF m's `votes in favour` AND `the paragraph of section 4(d) that a seat is in` (m's `the seat`) EQUALS paragraph THEN 1 ELSE 0)
        PLUS `the number in favour from a paragraph of section 4(d)` rest paragraph

GIVEN members IS A LIST OF `A member serving on the committee`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the number in favour from the three of section 4(f)(1)` MEANS
    CONSIDER members
    WHEN EMPTY THEN 0
    WHEN m FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        (IF m's `votes in favour` AND `the seat is one of the three of section 4(f)(1)` (m's `the seat`) THEN 1 ELSE 0)
        PLUS `the number in favour from the three of section 4(f)(1)` rest

§§ `May the committee act, and is there a quorum (s 4(c))`

-- s 4(c), both vintages: הועדה רשאית לפעול אף אם פחת מספר חבריה, כל עוד לא פחת משבעה.
-- The instrument (SH 3388 p. 434, s 1(2)) adds at the end of s 4(c): והמניין החוקי בישיבותיה הוא חמישה חברים. The consolidation OMITS that sentence: a consolidation error.
@ref Basic Law: The Judiciary s 4(c); SH 3388 p. 434 s 1(2)
GIVEN `the number of members serving` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the committee may act with this many members` MEANS
    `the number of members serving` AT LEAST 7

@ref Basic Law: The Judiciary s 4(c) as amended by Amendment No. 4 s 1(2); SH 3388 p. 434
GIVEN `the number of members at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a meeting of the committee has a quorum` MEANS
    `the number of members at the meeting` AT LEAST 5

§§ `The majority for a decision (s 4(d), (e), (f))`

-- s 4(d): החלטה של הוועדה תתקבל ברוב של חמישה חברים ובהם אחד מהמנויים בכל אחת מפסקאות (1) עד (3) שלהלן, המכהנים בוועדה
-- s 4(d), last words: והכול כשאין בחוק יסוד זה הוראה אחרת לעניין זה או אם נקבע בחוק רוב גדול יותר.
-- s 4(e): על אף האמור בסעיף קטן (ד) רישה, בחירת הוועדה בשופט לבית המשפט העליון – תהיה ברוב של חמישה חברים ובהם אחד מהמנויים בסעיף קטן (ד)(2) ואחד מהמנויים בסעיף קטן (ד)(3).
-- s 4(f): where the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members: (1) the members that are ministers and the Knesset member of the coalition factions are each from another faction,
--   and a decision must be with the consent of two of them; (2) the Knesset chooses both public representatives; (3) notwithstanding (d) and (e), a decision need not be with the consent of the Knesset member named in (d)(3).
-- s 4(d), last words, lets a law set a greater majority; this module encodes the Basic Law's own majorities only (fork D1 in NOTES.md).
@ref Basic Law: The Judiciary s 4(d), s 4(e), s 4(f)(1), (3); SH 3388 p. 434
GIVEN members IS A LIST OF `A member serving on the committee`
      kind IS A `A kind of decision of the committee`
      `the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the majority of section 4 is met` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `the election of a judge of the Supreme Court` THEN
        IF `the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members`
        THEN `the number voting in favour` members AT LEAST 5
             AND `the number in favour from the three of section 4(f)(1)` members AT LEAST 2
        ELSE `the number voting in favour` members AT LEAST 5
             AND `the number in favour from a paragraph of section 4(d)` members `paragraph 2, a minister, a Knesset member of the coalition factions, or the public representative the coalition Knesset members chose` AT LEAST 1
             AND `the number in favour from a paragraph of section 4(d)` members `paragraph 3, a Knesset member of the opposition factions, or the public representative the opposition Knesset members chose` AT LEAST 1
    WHEN `the election of a judge of a court other than the Supreme Court` THEN `the ordinary majority of section 4(d)` members `the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members`
    WHEN `a decision that is not the election of a judge` THEN `the ordinary majority of section 4(d)` members `the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members`

GIVEN members IS A LIST OF `A member serving on the committee`
      `the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the ordinary majority of section 4(d)` MEANS
    IF `the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members`
    THEN `the number voting in favour` members AT LEAST 5
         AND `the number in favour from a paragraph of section 4(d)` members `paragraph 1, a judge` AT LEAST 1
         AND `the number in favour from the three of section 4(f)(1)` members AT LEAST 2
    ELSE `the number voting in favour` members AT LEAST 5
         AND `the number in favour from a paragraph of section 4(d)` members `paragraph 1, a judge` AT LEAST 1
         AND `the number in favour from a paragraph of section 4(d)` members `paragraph 2, a minister, a Knesset member of the coalition factions, or the public representative the coalition Knesset members chose` AT LEAST 1
         AND `the number in favour from a paragraph of section 4(d)` members `paragraph 3, a Knesset member of the opposition factions, or the public representative the opposition Knesset members chose` AT LEAST 1

-- s 4(f)(1), first half: the members that are ministers and the coalition Knesset member are each from another faction. A fact about the people who sit, given as an input.
@ref Basic Law: The Judiciary s 4(f)(1); SH 3388 p. 434
GIVEN `the three are each from a different faction` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the composition meets section 4(f)(1)` MEANS
    IF `the coalition factions number more than 80 Knesset members`
    THEN `the three are each from a different faction`
    ELSE TRUE

§ `Section 4A: a deadlock over two Supreme Court seats`

-- s 4A(a)(1): על אף האמור בסעיף 4(ה), הסתיימה כהונתם של שני שופטים של בית המשפט העליון וחלפה שנה מיום שהסתיימה כהונתו של הראשון מהם או מיום תחילת כהונתה של כנסת חדשה, לפי המאוחר,
--   ובחלוף אותה שנה הוועדה לבחירת שופטים התכנסה לשם בחירת שופטים במקומם ובהצבעה שנערכה בה לא נבחר שופט, רשאי שר המשפטים להחליט כי בחירת שני שופטים במקומם תהיה בהתאם להוראות סעיף זה.
-- s 4A(a)(2): once only in the term of that Knesset, and notice of the decision is published in Reshumot.
-- The vintage is the text from the 26th Knesset; 4A is not in force before it.
GIVEN day IS A `A calendar day`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the serial number of a calendar day` MEANS
    Day (Date (day's `the day of the month`) (day's `the month`) (day's `the year`))

GIVEN day IS A `A calendar day`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the serial number of the same day a year later` MEANS
    Day (Date (day's `the day of the month`) (day's `the month`) ((day's `the year`) PLUS 1))

GIVEN day IS A `A calendar day`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the serial number of the same day a month later` MEANS
    IF day's `the month` EQUALS 12
    THEN Day (Date (day's `the day of the month`) 1 ((day's `the year`) PLUS 1))
    ELSE Day (Date (day's `the day of the month`) ((day's `the month`) PLUS 1) (day's `the year`))

@ref Basic Law: The Judiciary s 4A(a)(1), (2); SH 3388 p. 435
GIVEN `the first of the two terms ended on` IS A `A calendar day`
      `the term of the new Knesset began on` IS A `A calendar day`
      `the committee voted after that year and elected no judge, on` IS A MAYBE `A calendar day`
      `the Minister has already decided under 4A in this Knesset` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister of Justice may decide that section 4A applies` MEANS
    NOT `the Minister has already decided under 4A in this Knesset`
    AND CONSIDER `the committee voted after that year and elected no judge, on`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST voteDay THEN
            `the serial number of a calendar day` voteDay AT LEAST `the serial number of the same day a year later` (`the later of two days` `the first of the two terms ended on` `the term of the new Knesset began on`)

GIVEN a IS A `A calendar day`
      b IS A `A calendar day`
GIVETH A `A calendar day`
`the later of two days` MEANS
    IF `the serial number of a calendar day` a AT LEAST `the serial number of a calendar day` b THEN a ELSE b

-- s 4A(d)(1): after a month in which none of the proposed candidates was chosen, the members who proposed them may choose one of them.
@ref Basic Law: The Judiciary s 4A(d)(1); SH 3388 p. 435
GIVEN `the candidates were proposed on` IS A `A calendar day`
      day IS A `A calendar day`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the proposers may choose from their own candidates` MEANS
    `the serial number of a calendar day` day AT LEAST `the serial number of the same day a month later` `the candidates were proposed on`

§ `Section 4B: the periods when the committee may not elect judges`

-- s 4B: בתקופה שתחילתה באחד המועדים שלהלן ועד שייבחרו לוועדה חברים במקום החברים המנויים בסעיף 4(ב)(1)(ב) עד (ד), לא תבחר הוועדה שופטים; החלטות אחרות של הוועדה בתקופה כאמור יתקבלו על דעת כל החברים המכהנים בוועדה:
--   (1) מהיום ה־90 שלפני יום הבחירות לכנסת לפי סעיף 9 לחוק־יסוד: הכנסת; (2) מיום היווצרות עילה לקיום בחירות לפי סעיף 34 או 36א לחוק־יסוד: הכנסת או לפי סעיף 11(ב) או 29(ו) לחוק־יסוד: הממשלה;
--   (3) מיום התפטרות הממשלה לפי סעיפים 18, 19, 20, 21 או 29(א) לחוק־יסוד: הממשלה; (4) מיום ההחלטה של הכנסת להביע אי־אמון בממשלה לפי סעיף 28 לחוק־יסוד: הממשלה.
-- READING TAKEN (fork E1 in NOTES.md): the bar runs through the day before the day members are chosen; on the day they are chosen it no longer applies. A start day counts as part of the period.
GIVEN start IS A MAYBE DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a starting day has arrived by` MEANS
    CONSIDER start
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST s THEN Day day AT LEAST Day s

@ref Basic Law: The Judiciary s 4B(1) to (4); SH 3388 pp. 435-436
GIVEN days IS A `The days relevant to section 4B`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a starting day of section 4B has arrived by` MEANS
    `a starting day has arrived by` (`ninety days before` (days's `the day of the Knesset elections under s 9 of Basic Law: The Knesset`)) day
    OR `a starting day has arrived by` (days's `the day a ground for elections arose under s 34 or 36A of Basic Law: The Knesset, or s 11(b) or 29(f) of Basic Law: The Government`) day
    OR `a starting day has arrived by` (days's `the day the Government resigned under s 18, 19, 20, 21 or 29(a) of Basic Law: The Government`) day
    OR `a starting day has arrived by` (days's `the day the Knesset decided to express no confidence in the Government under s 28 of Basic Law: The Government`) day

@ref Basic Law: The Judiciary s 4B, opening words ("until members are chosen in place of ..."); SH 3388 p. 435
GIVEN days IS A `The days relevant to section 4B`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the members have not yet been chosen by` MEANS
    CONSIDER days's `the day members were chosen in place of the members named in s 4(b)(1)(b) to (d)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST chosen THEN Day day LESS THAN Day chosen

@ref Basic Law: The Judiciary s 4B; SH 3388 pp. 435-436
GIVEN days IS A `The days relevant to section 4B`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 4B bars the election of judges on` MEANS
    `a starting day of section 4B has arrived by` days day
    AND `the members have not yet been chosen by` days day

GIVEN election IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`ninety days before` MEANS
    CONSIDER election
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST e THEN JUST (Date ((Day e) MINUS 90))

-- s 4B, after the colon: other decisions in such a period are taken with the consent of all the members serving.
@ref Basic Law: The Judiciary s 4B; SH 3388 p. 435
GIVEN members IS A LIST OF `A member serving on the committee`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`all the members serving consent` MEANS
    `the number voting in favour` members EQUALS `the number of members serving` members

§ `What the committee may do on a day, by vintage`

-- Amendment No. 4 s 3 (SH 3388 p. 436, read from the page image): the Law begins on the first day of the 26th Knesset's term; from that day until a committee is set up under it,
-- the committee set up before commencement goes on, the old text applies to it, "provided that the committee shall not elect judges, and its other decisions in that period shall be
-- with the consent of all the members serving". The day the 26th Knesset's term begins and the day the new committee is set up are inputs the caller states (fork V1 in NOTES.md).
@ref Amendment No. 4 s 3 (commencement and application); SH 3388 p. 436
GIVEN day IS A DATE
      `the 26th Knesset's term begins on` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `a committee is set up under the new text on` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `A vintage of the committee rule`
`the vintage that applies on` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the 26th Knesset's term begins on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the text before the 26th Knesset`
    WHEN JUST begins THEN
        IF Day day LESS THAN Day begins
        THEN `the text before the 26th Knesset`
        ELSE CONSIDER `a committee is set up under the new text on`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN `the transitional window of Amendment No. 4 section 3`
             WHEN JUST setUp THEN
                 IF Day day LESS THAN Day setUp
                 THEN `the transitional window of Amendment No. 4 section 3`
                 ELSE `the text from the 26th Knesset`

@ref Amendment No. 4 s 3; SH 3388 p. 436
GIVEN vintage IS A `A vintage of the committee rule`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the committee may elect judges in this vintage` MEANS
    NOT (vintage EQUALS `the transitional window of Amendment No. 4 section 3`)

§ `Section 7(4): ending a judge's term by decision of the committee`

-- s 7(4): על פי החלטה של הועדה לבחירת שופטים שהציע יושב ראש הועדה, נציב תלונות הציבור על שופטים או נשיא בית המשפט העליון ושנתקבלה ברוב של שבעה חברים לפחות
-- The text is the same before and after the 26th Knesset. In the transitional window s 3 adds that other decisions are with all the members serving.
@ref Basic Law: The Judiciary s 7(4)
GIVEN proposer IS A `Who proposes to end a judge's term`
      members IS A LIST OF `A member serving on the committee`
      vintage IS A `A vintage of the committee rule`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the committee's decision ends the judge's term` MEANS
    NOT (proposer EQUALS `someone else`)
    AND `the number voting in favour` members AT LEAST 7
    AND (IF vintage EQUALS `the transitional window of Amendment No. 4 section 3`
         THEN `all the members serving consent` members
         ELSE TRUE)

-- s 5: לא יתמנה שופט אלא אזרח ישראל.
@ref Basic Law: The Judiciary s 5
GIVEN `the person is an Israeli citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person may be appointed a judge, as to citizenship` MEANS
    `the person is an Israeli citizen`
